thode bars, fabricated sections, track shoes, sheet piles, sin beams, and value-added billets and blooms. In addition, it is involved in design and manufacturing of EOT and gantry cranes for steel plants, ports, infrastructure, and heavy engineering applications; manufactures pressure-retaining equipment for high-pressure and high-temperature industrial applications; and manufactures ferrous cast components for metallurgical and thermal processing industries. Further, the company engages in the operation of iron ore mines in Kasia, Roida, and Tensa in India; coal assets; pellet plants; and captive power facilities. It serves infrastructure, distribution, automotive, defense, building and construction, and engineering and packing. The company was formerly known as Jindal Steel & Power Limited and changed its name to Jindal Steel Limited in July 2025. Jindal Steel Limited was incorporated in 1979 and is based in New Delhi, India.","beta":0.658,"sharesOutstanding":1017972361,"marketCap":1178608467968,"trailingPE":41.0859,"forwardPE":13.6743,"priceToBook":2.25,"enterpriseToEbitda":14.506,"dividendYield":0.17,"heldPercentInsiders":0.6385,"heldPercentInstitutions":0.2374,"earningsGrowth":0.212,"revenueGrowth":0.427,"website":"https://www.jindalsteel.in","fullTimeEmployees":5796,"recommendationKey":"none","targetMeanPrice":1206.4839,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":31,"financialCurrency":"INR"},"estimates":{"eps":{"0q":{"avg":11.1608,"low":11.1608,"high":11.1608,"yearAgoEps":2.1798,"numberOfAnalysts":1.0,"growth":4.1201,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"+1q":{"avg":11.1608,"low":11.1608,"high":11.1608,"yearAgoEps":18.1062,"numberOfAnalysts":1.0,"growth":-0.3836,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"0y":{"avg":55.4036,"low":45.5588,"high":71.0,"yearAgoEps":39.6948,"numberOfAnalysts":28.0,"growth":0.3957,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"+1y":{"avg":84.6697,"low":69.8,"high":104.2,"yearAgoEps":55.4036,"numberOfAnalysts":28.0,"growth":0.5282,"currency